2026-05-22 14:35:10,342 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent received: The solution must guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR), with data hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the EU authorized, and sensitive data protected in an appropriate manner. How can we ensure security and regulatory compliance, and what measures do we propose?
2026-05-22 14:36:11,186 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-05-22 14:36:11,186 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To ensure security and regulatory compliance under GDPR, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. proposes the following measures. Our standard data residency is EU only, aligning with the requirement for data to be hosted exclusively within the European Union territory. We prohibit cross-border transfers by default unless there's an explicit legal basis for doing so, ensuring that no unauthorized transfer of data outside the EU occurs.

For sensitive data protection, we utilize anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models to ensure that personal data is appropriately protected. We have also implemented various data subject rights including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection, facilitating compliance with GDPR requirements.

Moreover, our Data Protection Officer (DPO) can be contacted at dpo@nexus-engineering.it for any matters related to data protection. We conduct Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) with an average duration of 3 weeks, which helps in identifying and mitigating risks associated with the processing of personal data.

We enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), and our Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) design experience ensures that access to data is strictly controlled. Session timeouts are set at 30 minutes, adding an extra layer of security.

Our network security architecture follows zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth patterns, with Intrusion Detection/Prevention Systems (IDS/IPS) deployed. Annual penetration testing plus post-major release testing, conducted by partners like Synacktiv and HN Security, helps identify vulnerabilities.

For AI security controls, we have measures in place such as prompt injection protection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, confidence threshold escalation, model isolation (inference API only), and model update security reviews to protect against potential AI-related risks.

All queries are logged with log immutability ensured through append-only logging with SHA-256 hash chaining. Audit logs are retained for 7 years, and we have the capability for CNIL export as well as real-time SIEM integration using tools like Wazuh and Elastic SIEM.

Lastly, our Security Incident Response Team (SIRT) is in place with breach notification procedures that adhere to the 72-hour delay requirement. We conduct semi-annual drills to ensure readiness and have playbooks available for incident response scenarios.

By implementing these measures, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. ensures a high level of security and compliance with GDPR regulations, providing assurance that data hosted within our systems is protected appropriately and in accordance with EU law.
